; Bug repro: a consumer that imports a whole library (no `from`
; clause) and references a non-exported private helper from
; that library must NOT trigger a W006 "unused library export"
; warning.  A library export is a public API surface, not an
; obligation for every consumer of the library to reference
; every exported name.  Before the fix, W006 falsely fired for
; the unused `public-a` export.
;
; Expected after fix:
; - W003 may fire (consumer uses non-exported `private-helper`).
; - no W004 (the directive IS used).
; - no W005 (no selected names).
; - no W006 (whole-library import, unused export is not an
;   obligation).

;# import "./support/bug_002_whole_lib.cddl" as bug_002_lib

ok = bug_002_lib.private-helper
